VERDICT
====================================================================================================
  THE PHASE PINS.  Mechanism: the AeST dust is a gamma=2 polytrope, p_d = (2 pi G/mu^2) rho_d^2, with c_s^2 = |Psi| c^2 in a well;
  DS24's Helmholtz 'phase' is its Bernoulli constant = captured mass; every node-bearing branch has rho_d<0 <=> c_s^2<0 and is
  gradient-unstable; the unique admissible configuration is the positive polytrope with a free surface R_s < pi/mu, and the
  time-dependent gamma=2 hydro lands on it and forgets the IC phase (F3).  The June 'no pin' evolved the gapped branch (B1).
  THE PINNED YIELD (canonical, DS24 kernel): core dust 3.19e+13 Msun = 32% of the 1e14 residual (21% of 1.5e14), eta(R500) = 3.17; band over footings/kernels 23-33%.
  AGAINST INTEREST: the same configuration gives eta(R500) = 2.57 (framework kernel) / 3.17 (DS24) vs observed 2.33 raw, 1.7 WL-corrected:
  it OVERSHOOTS R500 while UNDERSHOOTING the core; normalised to the observed R500 the core is 20% (raw) / 14% (WL).
  Galaxy-safe by geometry (E1).  The binding limit is the SHAPE (rho_d ∝ C - Psi cannot concentrate into a 420 kpc core), not the amount.
  The lever exists only at AeST's phenomenological mu^-1 = 1 Mpc (D11); at the framework's own Q-sector mass it is nil.
  => The |Phi| lever is REAL, PREDICTIVE (no per-cluster tune), GALAXY-SAFE, and NOT A CLOSURE: the cluster core gap stays >= 65% open.
  CORRECTS: the published no-go's 'c_s^2 -> 0 => density-ordered clumping' premise (wrong in wells) and its 'single un-closed branch = 3D N-body' (closed here).

